course: dictionary
lesson: 185
title: Aim: goal or target
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: The word «aim» has two main jobs. As a noun it means your goal, what you are trying to get or do. As a verb it means to point something at a target. Context tells you which one: «The aim of the game is to score the most points» names a goal, while «Aim the ball at the goal» tells you to point it.
explain: Look at the words near aim for clues. Words like «at», «for» and «to» often come after it: aim at a target, aim for a prize, aim to finish. «Take aim» is a phrase that means getting ready and pointing carefully before you throw or shoot.
explain: In school you will meet «learning aim» or «learning intention». Here aim means the goal of the lesson: what you should understand by the end. Swap in your meaning to check it. If "goal" fits the sentence, you have the right meaning.
fact: Aim can be a noun (an aim, aims) or a verb (aim, aims, aimed, aiming).
fact: As a noun, aim means your goal or purpose: «What is the aim of this experiment?»
fact: As a verb, aim means to point at something you want to hit or reach, or to plan to do something: «We aim to finish by lunch.»
fact: «Aimed at» means meant for a particular person or group: «The book is aimed at children.»
fact: Safety: never aim a stick, a toy gun, a hose or a laser at someone's face or eyes.
exercise: «In science, every experiment starts with an aim.» What is the aim of an experiment? | *What we want to find out | A loud noise made by the class | A pointed stick used to hit a ball
exercise: «Aim water guns at the body, not the face.» What does aim mean here? | To forget about something | To clean it up | *To point it carefully at something | To shout loudly
exercise: «The book is aimed at children.» What does aimed at mean? | Hidden from | *Meant for a particular group | Shouting to | Thrown hard at
test: «The aim of the game is to score the most points.» In this sentence, aim is a | *noun, meaning a goal | verb, meaning to point | adverb | adjective
test: Ava says, «I aim to be a doctor.» What does aim mean? | To hide under a bed | *To plan or try to do something | To be wrong and unfair | To point a camera at a friend
exam: Which is the safest way to use a toy water gun? | Aim it at a teacher who is not playing | Point it at the sky and forget about it | *Aim it at the body of a friend who is playing too | Aim it at a friend's face to make them laugh
